</table>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 1: </span>Average eigenbasis similarity (top-<math id="S4.T1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=8</annotation></semantics></math>) between retain and forget PEMs across layers.</figcaption>
</figure>
<section id="S4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.1 </span>Preliminary Study</h3>

<div id="S4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We first conduct a preliminary analysis to quantify the overlap between the <span id="S4.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">retain</span> and <span id="S4.SS1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">forget</span> PEMs. For each layer, we obtain the merged LoRA update matrix <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W=BA" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W=BA</annotation></semantics></math>, and compute its top-<math id="S4.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> left singular vectors via SVD:</p>
<table id="S4.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{\text{retain}}=U_{1}\Sigma_{1}V_{1}^{\top},\quad W_{\text{forget}}=U_{2}\Sigma_{2}V_{2}^{\top}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mtext>retain</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mtext>forget</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{\text{retain}}=U_{1}\Sigma_{1}V_{1}^{\top},\quad W_{\text{forget}}=U_{2}\Sigma_{2}V_{2}^{\top},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{1}^{(k)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{1}^{(k)}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{2}^{(k)}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{2}^{(k)}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times k}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the top-<math id="S4.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> left singular vectors.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">To measure the similarity between the subspaces, we compute:</p>
<table id="S4.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Sim}(U_{1}^{(k)},U_{2}^{(k)})=\frac{1}{k}\left\|{U_{1}^{(k)}}^{\top}U_{2}^{(k)}\right\|_{F}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>Sim</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>k</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mmultiscripts><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></mmultiscripts><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Sim}(U_{1}^{(k)},U_{2}^{(k)})=\frac{1}{k}\left\|{U_{1}^{(k)}}^{\top}U_{2}^{(k)}\right\|_{F},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S4.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\|\cdot\|_{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\cdot\|_{F}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the Frobenius norm. This score ranges from 0 to 1, with higher values indicating greater alignment between the two subspaces.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.T2" class="ltx_table">
<table id="S4.T2.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="S4.T2.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S4.T2.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_th_row ltx_border_r ltx_border_t"><span id="S4.T2.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Model</span></th>
<th id="S4.T2.2.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_th_row ltx_border_r ltx_border_t"><span id="S4.T2.2.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">PPL <math id="S4.T2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\downarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">↓</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\downarrow</annotation></semantics></math></span></th>
<th id="S4.T2.2.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_r ltx_border_t" colspan="3"><span id="S4.T2.2.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Challenge</span></th>
<th id="S4.T2.2.1.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_t" colspan="3"><span id="S4.T2.2.1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Non-Challenge</span></th></tr>
<tr id="S4.T2.2.2" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S4.T2.2.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_th_row ltx_border_r"></th>
<th id="S4.T2.2.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_th_row ltx_border_r"></th>
<th id="S4.T2.2.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column">Tox. Score <math id="S4.T2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\downarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">↓</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\downarrow</annotation></semantics></math></th>
<th id="S4.T2.2.2.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column">Tox. Rate <math id="S4.T2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\downarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">↓</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\downarrow</annotation></semantics></math></th>
