<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 10: </span>Study on the effect of orthogonality loss in NER unlearning. Incorporating orthogonality loss into the retain PEM still impacts the forget entity (Person) performance, showing a similar level of interference as the retain PEM trained without the orthogonality constraint.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Results on Mistral-7B-Instruct-v0.2</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To further validate the generalizability of our approach, we conducted additional experiments on all three unlearning tasks using Mistral-7B-Instruct-v0.2, following the same protocol as with LLaMA3-8B-Instruct. The results show that our method consistently achieves effective unlearning across different model families, as shown in Table <a href="#A3.T11" title="Table 11 ‣ Appendix C Results on Mistral-7B-Instruct-v0.2 ‣ Reveal and Release: Iterative LLM Unlearning with Self-generated Data" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a>, Table <a href="#A3.T12" title="Table 12 ‣ Appendix C Results on Mistral-7B-Instruct-v0.2 ‣ Reveal and Release: Iterative LLM Unlearning with Self-generated Data" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a>, and Table <a href="#A3.T13" title="Table 13 ‣ Appendix C Results on Mistral-7B-Instruct-v0.2 ‣ Reveal and Release: Iterative LLM Unlearning with Self-generated Data" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a>.</p>
</div>
